{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788281198,"nonce":"2Ov8gZPq69OJfbeHsXf6XVNavFg=","message":"PROVEN ON A LIVE BENCH — CLOSING, with one bullet marked unreachable rather\nthan met. Session 16, 2026-09-01, assembly `479e4a1`.\n\n**`buildable:true` runs the real gate.** On a cell the god-hand had just\naccepted, the opt-in refused:\n\n    dev:spawn-thing {def:\"Wall\", pos:[118,130], mode:\"direct\"}            -\u003e placed\n    dev:spawn-thing {def:\"Wall\", pos:[118,130], mode:\"direct\", buildable} -\u003e placed 0\n        reason \"Identical thing already exists here.\"  cell_role \"footprint\"\n\n`IdenticalThingExists` is a `CanPlaceBlueprintAt` check that `GenSpawn.CanSpawnAt`\ndoes not have at all, so this is not the same validator being stricter — it is\nthe other validator.\n\n**`site-audit` catches exactly what it exists for.** Staged the pair this issue\ndescribes — two research benches whose interaction cells coincide, placed\ngod-hand — and audited:\n\n    scanned 3, hit_count 2\n    HIT {id:18470, def:\"SimpleResearchBench\", at:[125,127], rot:\"North\",\n         footprint:{at:[124,127],w:3,h:2},\n         reason:\"Interaction spot overlaps with the interaction spot of wooden…\"}\n    HIT {id:18471, … at:[125,125], rot:\"South\", …same reason}\n\nEach with the sentence `site-survey` gives for the same site — the acceptance's\n\"each with the reason `dev:spawn-thing {buildable:true}` gave\". A clean area\naudits `hit_count: 0`. The result carries the caveat the issue demanded,\nverbatim: *\"a hit means CHECK THIS, not 'this is fake': a real game legitimately\nreaches states the blueprint validator would now refuse.\"*\n\n**The starter-kit regression is closed.** `dev:starter-kit --preset medical`\nstaged two beds and both survived. Doing this issue's item 3 literally —\n`mode:\"direct\"` with the existing `count` loop — would have run the stack loop\ntwice against one cell, and `GenSpawn.SpawningWipes(Bed, Bed)` is true for two\nedifices, so the second bed would have vanished the first while the envelope\nreported `placed: 2`. `Near` mode was hiding that by scattering them. One call\nper unit, distinct gated cells.\n\n**The two other fixture routes carry the gate**, and one of them needed a\nfollow-up: `world-fixture bench` refused on its second call because the gate\nlanded without the site SEARCH sharing it. Fixed in `479e4a1`; see `0d9cbd7`.\n`journal-selftest power` passes.\n\n\nThe bullet asks for `dev:spawn-thing {def:\"Wall\", buildable:false}` onto a rock\nwall to place and report `wiped[0]` naming the rock. It cannot:\n`GenSpawn.CanSpawnAt` tests `!c.Walkable(map)` on **`c`, the CENTRE cell**,\ninside the loop over the occupied rect, so any unwalkable occupant returns false\nbefore `canWipeEdifices` is consulted. Four attempts, all *\"the cell is not\nwalkable\"* — including the bullet's own rock-wall case. A fifth (a Wall over a\nlive blueprint, which IS walkable) placed and reported `wiped: []` correctly,\nbecause `SpawningWipes` does not name that pair.\n\nSo the field is published and honest — `[]` on a spawn that erased nothing,\n`null` on a refusal — and the reachable set is far smaller than this issue\nassumes: the occupant must leave the centre cell walkable while still being\nsomething `SpawningWipes` names. Detail and the four measurements are in the\ncomment above. **Closing rather than leaving open, because the code is correct\nand it is the acceptance text that is wrong**; if the wipe path is worth\ncovering it wants a new issue with a case that can actually occur.","files":null}]}